# Cases for core-language-docs/core.md. Read by ../run-all.sh, which
# discovers every */CASES under snippets/ rather than carrying a list.
#
# Five pipe-separated fields:
#
#   module | cfg | expected-rc | distinct-states | what it shows
#
# A blank line or a line opening with # is skipped.
#
# THE FOURTH FIELD IS THE STATE COUNT, and it is not decoration. Two of this
# page's findings are counts across runs that all exit 0. Vacuous.cfg and
# VacuousWitness.cfg both pass over the same 4 states, and that equality is
# what makes the first pass vacuous. RecHigher.cfg passes over 4 states, which
# is the evidence that a RECURSIVE higher-order operator computed the right
# answer four times rather than being accepted and never run. An rc-only
# suite would be green on both while the page went wrong.
#
# The field is empty on every case that fails, because a failed run stops
# where it fails and its count is an artifact of the search order.
#
# Exit codes TLC uses here. Four of the six are not in run-all.sh's own list,
# which was written against the modules page:
#   0    all checks passed
#   11   deadlock: a reachable state has no successor
#   12   an invariant was violated
#   75   evaluation failed before TLC had a behavior to show
#   76   evaluating an invariant failed, and TLC had a behavior to show
#   150  parse or semantic error in the module

